==Azerbaijani==
{{az-variant|пај|پای}}

===Etymology===
According to Nişanyan, from {{der|az|fa|پای|tr=pây||foot}}, with the sense ”share” originating from the {{w|Persian}} expression borrowed into   {{der|az|trk-oat|بای برابر|tr=pây-berâber||equally, to the same proportion|lit=equal foot}}. The word is present in its modern sense in XIVth century ''{{w|Book of Dede Korkut}}''.
The non-Oghuz Turkic cognates, such as {{w|Kirgiz}} and {{cog|sah|пай||share}} are, according to Nişanyan, a borrowing from the {{cog|ota|پای}}, via {{cog|ru|пай}}.
However it is more possibly borrowed from {{der|az|ltc|派|tr=pʰaiH}} as early as 7th century and inherited by later Turkic languages.

